# dxgi: Release the frame latency semaphore for occluded presents.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12437 state=merged
# Unity games wait on the frame latency waitable object before every \`Present()\`. When the window is minimized, \`d3d11_swapchain_present()\` returns \`DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED\` without queuing anything, so the semaphore is never released and the game hangs after minimize/restore.

This adds \`wined3d_swapchain_skip_present()\`, which queues the release on the command stream behind any pending presents, and calls it on the occluded path. It only applies to waitable swapchains and is skipped for \`DXGI_PRESENT_TEST\`. 

Tested with the dxgi, d3d11 and d3d10core tests and with ULTRAKILL, which no longer hangs.

Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=60111
